# Browser WebSocket messaging

This page starts after <GuideRef slug="clients/browser/setup-and-http">browser setup and HTTP</GuideRef>. Use the same initialized Wasm package and shared `Connection`; do not create a second package or duplicate target dependency setup for messaging.

Server controller destinations, endpoint mounting, protocol framing, and topic publication remain under <GuideRef slug="axum/websocket">Axum WebSocket</GuideRef>.

## Attach protocol transports

JSON-WS and STOMP export free functions; they are not methods on `Connection`:

```ts plain
import init, {
  ChatHandlerClient,
  ChatTopicClient,
  Connection,
  StompConnectOptions,
  connectJsonWs,
  connectStomp,
  disconnectJsonWs,
  disconnectStomp,
} from './pkg/catalog_api.js';

await init();
const connection = new Connection('https://api.example.test');

await connectJsonWs(connection, '/ws');
const alerts = new AlertSocketClient(connection);
await alerts.acknowledge({ id: 'alert-42' });
disconnectJsonWs(connection);
```

`connectJsonWs` attaches or replaces the `JsonWs` transport; `disconnectJsonWs` detaches it without a protocol-level graceful handshake. `AlertSocketClient` is a schema-shaped example because the committed fixture gates its JSON-WS controller out on Wasm. Use the names in your generated `.d.ts`.

## Connect STOMP and subscribe

```ts plain
const options = new StompConnectOptions();
options.setHost('catalog');
options.setLogin('worker');
options.setPasscode(secret);
options.addHeader('tenant', 'acme');
await connectStomp(connection, '/ws/stomp', options);

const topics = new ChatTopicClient(connection);
const subscription = await topics.subscribe_chat((message: ChatMessage) => {
  console.log(message.room, message.text);
});

const messages = new ChatHandlerClient(connection);
await messages.on_chat({
  room: 'general',
  sender: 'Ada',
  text: 'hello',
});

subscription.unsubscribe();
await disconnectStomp(connection);
```

`connectStomp` disconnects an existing STOMP transport, performs CONNECT/CONNECTED with the supplied options, and attaches the result. `disconnectStomp` gracefully disconnects and detaches it.

The committed `subscribe_chat` binding returns a `TopicSubscription`. Calling `unsubscribe()` or allowing the handle to be garbage-collected aborts the callback pump and drops that subscription; it does not disconnect the shared STOMP socket.

## Follow the generated ABI

`wasm-bindgen` retains emitted Rust method spellings such as `subscribe_chat` and `on_chat`. Treat the generated `.d.ts` as authoritative for client classes, callback payloads, method casing, and promise results.

<Callout type="warning" title="Browser handshake limits">

Browser WebSocket handshakes cannot set arbitrary headers. Put STOMP credentials and custom headers in CONNECT. Other authentication must use cookies, query parameters, or a server-supported negotiated subprotocol.

</Callout>

For native connection ownership and transport-specific shutdown, use <GuideRef slug="clients/native/websocket">native WebSocket clients</GuideRef>.
